r-dimension std, mean_pairwise_distance, fraction_unique) within 1\u20133 iterations, producing greater performance variance and enabling selection to find improved candidates (higher best and mean performance).", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "After the change, accept if the validator reports an improvement over current accepted state (expected signals: increase in best or mean performance and/or increased diversity). Monitor next 1\u20135 iterations for increases in best_performance (ideally >0) and diversity metrics (per_dimension_std_mean, fraction_unique, mean_pairwise_distance). If no meaningful improvement in 3\u20135 iterations, consider adding exploration objectives (parameter_spread) or increasing random_candidate_ratio.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.7, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "The population has collapsed toward the center and exploration is essentially disabled by optimizer settings (mutation_prob = 0.0 and random_candidate_ratio = 0.0). Increasing per-gene mutation probability is a low-risk, high-leverage change to restore search diversity quickly.\n\n<decision>{\n  \"failure_location\": \"optimization_workflow\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The optimizer's exploration settings are suppressing diversity \u2014 mutation_prob is at its lower bound (0.0) and random_candidate_ratio is 0.0, which, together with observed low per-dimension std (mean 0.01305) and low fraction_unique (0.125), caused contraction toward center and small performance spread.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"optimization_workflow\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Diagnostics show mutation_prob current=0.0 (at_lower_bound=true) and random_candidate_ratio=0.0, while diversity metrics are low (per_dimension_std_mean=0.01305, fraction_unique=0.125, mean_pairwise_distance=0.03794). Performance mean is very low (0.018824 \u00b1 0.001247) with small range. Enabling mutation should increase candidate variation and allow discovery of higher